      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.39,
      "end_seconds": 118.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "I'm on Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.88,
      "end_seconds": 121.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.11,
      "end_seconds": 126.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.29,
      "end_seconds": 144.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.43,
      "end_seconds": 151.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Yes, plasters. I get a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.06,
      "end_seconds": 156.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Alright, a few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.77,
      "end_seconds": 174.17,
      "duration_seconds": 16.4,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. My partner and our baby. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.61,
      "end_seconds": 190.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "let's start with the basic checks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.77,
      "end_seconds": 202.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.61,
      "end_seconds": 231.79,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.7 degrees, BMI works out to 30.7, saturation 96 percent. And BP is 166 over 100, height 151 centimetres, weight 70 kilos, pulse is 74 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.88,
      "end_seconds": 235.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.24,
      "end_seconds": 240.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.9,
      "end_seconds": 262.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "Going by what you've described, I think we're dealing with a diabetic foot ulcer with some circulation concern at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.45,
      "end_seconds": 265.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.5,
      "end_seconds": 293.03,
      "duration_seconds": 25.53,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a diabetic foot ulcer with some circulation concern do well once it's treated properly. An HbA1c is what I'd like next, for diabetes control that will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step look at your feet every day with a mirror and never go barefoot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.53,
      "end_seconds": 300.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. The podiatry clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.66,
      "end_seconds": 304.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Alright, uh, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.42,
      "end_seconds": 322.81,
      "duration_seconds": 17.39,
      "text": "One warning sign to remember: the sore becomes red, smelly or the foot turns dusky. In that case don't wait. I'd like to see you again in two weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.4,
      "end_seconds": 328.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "good, you know, thanks, I'll see you then"
    }
  ]
